Vendored build inputs for the Ubuntu PPA source package
========================================================

Launchpad's PPA build farm has no outbound network access, so anything the
build needs must be shipped inside the source package. This directory holds
the two large payloads that would otherwise have to be fetched over the
network mid-build.

flutter-3.44.6-linux-slim.tar.xz
--------------------------------
A Linux-only slice of the Flutter 3.44.6 stable SDK.

Started from the upstream tarball:

  https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/stable/linux/flutter_linux_3.44.6-stable.tar.xz

  Framework revision: ee80f08bbf97172ec030b8751ceab557177a34a6
  Engine revision:    83675ed27633283e7fc296c8bca22e841224c096
  Dart SDK:           3.12.2

Stripped, before repacking, of everything the `flutter build linux --release`
path does not touch:

  * bin/cache/artifacts/engine/{android-*,darwin-*,ios*,windows-*,linux-x64-profile}
  * bin/cache/flutter_web_sdk (Flutter web SDK)
  * bin/cache/artifacts/{gradle_wrapper,ios-*,libimobiledevice*,libplist,libusbmuxd,openssl}
  * dev/, examples/, docs/, agent-artifacts/
  * bin/cache/dart-sdk/bin/dartaotruntime_{a,m,t}san (sanitizer builds)
  * bin/cache/dart-sdk/bin/resources/{devtools,dartdoc}
  * Web-only Dart snapshots (dart2js, dart2wasm, dartdevc, kernel_worker, wasm-opt)
  * bin/cache/dart-sdk/bin/snapshots/analysis_server*.snapshot (IDE LSP support)
  * bin/cache/dart-sdk/bin/snapshots/dart_mcp_server_aot.dart.snapshot
  * *.sym debug symbol files
  * bin/cache/dart-sdk/bin/{dartvm.sym,dartvm} was stripped and then dartvm was
    restored because it is required by the Dart CLI dispatcher at runtime
  * .git (replaced with a minimal shim so the flutter shell script's
    `git rev-parse HEAD` still succeeds; combined with
    `FLUTTER_PREBUILT_ENGINE_VERSION` set in debian/rules, this is enough for
    the flutter tool to bootstrap without touching a real git history)

Uncompressed size:  ~653 MB
Compressed size:    ~147 MB (xz -6)

pub-cache-3.44.6.tar.xz
-----------------------
The subset of the pub.dev hosted cache that resolves the exact package
versions listed in pubspec.lock. Only the 77 hosted packages from
pubspec.lock are shipped, along with their matching sha256 hash files under
hosted-hashes/pub.dev/.

Populated by running `flutter pub get` once against the stripped Flutter SDK
above with a scratch PUB_CACHE, then copying only the pubspec.lock-resolved
package directories out.

Uncompressed size:  ~89 MB
Compressed size:    ~19 MB (xz -6)

How debian/rules uses these
---------------------------
1. Extract flutter-3.44.6-linux-slim.tar.xz into $(CURDIR)/.flutter/
2. Extract pub-cache-3.44.6.tar.xz into $(CURDIR)/.pub-cache/
3. Export FLUTTER_PREBUILT_ENGINE_VERSION so the flutter tool skips its git-
   based engine-version lookup (which does not work with the shim .git).
4. Run `flutter pub get --offline` (uses only the extracted pub cache).
5. Run `flutter build linux --release --no-pub` (skips the online pub
   check the build command would otherwise perform).

No step reaches the network.

Regenerating (only when bumping the Flutter version pin)
--------------------------------------------------------
This is not automated because it only happens on a version bump. Steps:

  1. Download the upstream Flutter Linux stable tarball for the new version.
  2. Extract and apply the prune list above.
  3. Recreate the minimal .git shim with the new framework revision:
       mkdir -p .git/refs/heads
       echo "ref: refs/heads/stable" > .git/HEAD
       echo "<framework-revision>" > .git/refs/heads/stable
  4. Repack with `tar -cJf flutter-<version>-linux-slim.tar.xz flutter/`.
  5. Rebuild the pub cache in the same session against a fresh project
     checkout so pubspec.lock is honoured.
  6. Update FLUTTER_VERSION and FLUTTER_ENGINE_VERSION in debian/rules to
     match the new pin.
